  "notes": "{赤|あか} is one of the basic Japanese color words. Can function as a noun, no-adjective, or the base of the i-adjective {赤|あか}い.\n\nFORMS:\n- Noun: {赤|あか}が{好|す}き (I like red)\n- No-adjective: {赤|あか}の{他人|たにん} (complete stranger)\n- I-adjective: {赤|あか}い{花|はな} (red flower)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {赤|あか}ちゃん: baby\n- {赤|あか}ワイン: red wine\n- {真|ま}っ{赤|か}: bright red; blatant (lie)\n- {赤|あか}の{他人|たにん}: complete stranger\n- {赤字|あかじ}: deficit, in the red\n\nIDIOM:\n{真|ま}っ{赤|か}な{嘘|うそ}: a blatant lie",
